 know anything about piano maybe  you don't love piano so how can you ever  be a great piano teacher and provide  that value what you need to do is think  about what are you really good at doing  what do you really love doing what would  you do in your part time what do you do  as a hobby if you didn't have this job  that you hate going to what would you do  with your day what makes you come alive  and then think about how can you help  people how can you turn what you  love into something that provides  tangible value for other people the more  you can help people the more money  you're going to make you want to make a  lot of money that helped a lot of people  you want to make a lot of money quickly  then help a lot of people quickly so  you've got to sit back and do a self  analysis really figure out what you love  and how you can use that love to help  somebody and I love the idea of you  starting part-time you don't need to  jump into this as a full-time business a  lot of people make that mistake they  quit their job they start their company  and then it takes way longer than they  thought it would for them to make some  money you start seeing your cash  reserves run out the bank account is  going dry and you have to go back and  get another job where it's way better  than start part-time build your business  up slowly and when you're making enough  that you can afford to leave your job  you're quits you can focus on your  business 100% so that's my advice to you  this year good luck and believe for  those of you watching my question for  you is how did you start your business  part-time what were the difficulties you  had what were some of the stresses you  had how did you manage that  with your job and your family leave a  comment below I'd really love to hear  from you about how you started that  business of yours part-time and if you  like this video and you want to see more  don't forget to subscribe to the channel  and to the newsletter thank you so much  for watching I'll see you soon
 

